# Contributing

How the course repository is built and how to change it. Using it: [README.md](README.md). Conventions that apply to
every project, with their reasons: [CONVENTIONS.md](CONVENTIONS.md) (a read-only copy of the guide; `copier update`
refreshes it). The `conventions-reviewer` subagent in `.claude/agents/` checks a branch or the repo against it.

## Layout

```text
src/{{ course }}/            shared by every lab: labs, latex, paths, report, storage,
                          cli ({{ cli }} configs | report)
src/nuikit/               copied from the conventions template: config, configgen, registry, errors, logging,
                          runs, seeding; change it upstream and `copier update`
labs/NNN-topic/           one uv workspace member per lab, package labNNN, created by `make lab`
  config/main.yaml        generated from src/labNNN/config.py by `make configs`
  config/hydra/           Hydra settings: runs keep their resolved config in outputs/<script>/<time>/.hydra/
  src/labNNN/             the lab's pure computations and its config schemas
  scripts/                Hydra entry points: load config, call src/, write data/ and report values
  tests/                  invariant tests plus a subprocess smoke test of each script
  data/raw/               committed inputs; everything else in data/ is regenerated
  report/report.tex       \input{generated/values}: numbers come from the pipeline, never typed
latex/                    TeX Live Dockerfile, latexmkrc, lab-report.cls, course.tex (title page values)
tests/                    tests of the shared package; tests/nuikit/ comes with the template
```

## A lab's pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    yaml["config/main.yaml"]:::pure --> script["scripts/run.py"]:::side
    raw["data/raw/"]:::side --> script
    script --> compute["src/labNNN/<br/>pure computations"]:::pure
    script --> data["data/*.json, *.parquet"]:::side
    script --> values["report/generated/values.tex"]:::side
    values --> pdf["make report<br/>report.pdf"]:::side
    classDef pure fill:#d9f2ec,stroke:#1b7f6b,color:#0b3d33
    classDef side fill:#f8e3d8,stroke:#b4532a,color:#4a1f0c
```

- Parameters come from the lab's config, never from constants in code. Add a `Field(default=..., description=...)`
  to the schema in `src/labNNN/config.py`, then run `make configs`.
- Storage format follows the data's role: CSV raw, parquet derived tables, JSON metrics, NPZ arrays (`Storage`).
- Report numbers go through `report.number()` and `report.write_values()`; figures go to `report/generated/figures/`.
- Identifiers, comments and docstrings are English; report text, plot labels and messages for graders may be
  Ukrainian.

## Adding a lab

```bash
make lab N=002 TOPIC=spark-graphs     # renders the lab template, adds it to the workspace
git switch -c lab/002-spark-graphs
```

## Tests

```bash
make test     # shared package + every lab
```

Tests check invariants (shapes, monotonicity, conservation), never values copied from config. Each script has a
subprocess smoke test on a tiny config in `tmp_path`.

## Commits

Conventional Commits with the standard types and the lab as scope: `feat(lab002): add GraphFrames motif search`.
One line, no articles, no body. Branches are `lab/NNN-topic` and squash-merge as `feat(labNNN): <title>`.
